# `EffectivePluginPlan`

<SymbolMeta />

`EffectivePluginPlan` is the immutable plugin record attached to a prepared application and runtime application. It is the authoritative record of selected structure and plugin emissions, before or alongside the final application registry's own view.

<SymbolSignature />

## Inspection

`resolution` exposes deterministic effective plugins, slot selections, replacement decisions, and suppressions through the resolved plan. `emitted_contributions` preserves resolution order and each contributor-local emission order. Together they let tooling distinguish an installed plugin from an emission that was later displaced or rejected while the registry was lowered.

Read the plan from `PreparedApp::plugin_plan` or `App::plugin_plan`; do not reconstruct selection from registration calls. Cargo Upwell projects the same preparation facts into `inspect`, `explain`, graph, and export workflows.

Use [Inspect the effective plan](/docs/latest/extensions/plugins#inspect-the-effective-plan) for command-line diagnosis and [Inspect and query an application](/docs/latest/cargo-upwell/inspect-and-graph) for selectors and machine output.

<SymbolMembers />
